<title>USA: U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 6.328 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 6.328 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 2-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 2-YEAR NOTES DUE MAY 31, 1999</p>
<p>			     $16.501 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.328    Awarded At	99.856	6.250</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.312    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 6.280    42 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.43 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 31.May.99</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    2-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 02.Jun.97</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 28.May.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  16.501 BLN USD		 CUSIP   9128272V3</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   40.027			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE    1.410				DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.250</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   1.360			   PRICE	 99.856</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    6.280-6.328 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   6.328</p>
<p> KEY (HIGH) YIELD DOWN FROM 6.46 PCT AT AUCTION ON 22.APR.97</p>
<p> KEY (HIGH) YIELD LOWEST SINCE 6.270 PCT AT AUCTION 25.MAR.97</p>
</text>
